<workout_file><author>mywhooshinfo.com</author><name>Lactate Tolerance #2</name><description>Riding at threshold power for sustained periods will require a significant lactate production. To reach this lactate level in a shorter workout requires brief periods of work above threshold, with minimal recovery. 

With each interval, the lactate levels will rise.</description><sportType>bike</sportType><workout>
<Warmup  Duration="600" PowerLow="0.44449999928474" PowerHigh="0.75449997186661"></Warmup>
<SteadyState  Duration="60" Power="0.55000001192093"></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="60" Power="1.1100000143051"></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="60" Power="0.55000001192093"></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.85000002384186"></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.55000001192093"></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="3" OnDuration="120" OnPower="1.210000038147" OffDuration="120" OffPower="0.5">
</IntervalsT>
<SteadyState  Duration="900" Power="0.69999998807907"></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="120" Power="0.55000001192093"></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="3" OnDuration="120" OnPower="1.210000038147" OffDuration="120" OffPower="0.5">
</IntervalsT>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.5"></SteadyState>
</workout></workout_file>